title One core, many shapes
sub nodes, paths that end in => or =|, and a view

== graph Call stack
view: stack
main: main() [frame] @app/main.ts:3
  locals: argv = ["--qty", "x"]
parse: parseArgs(argv) [frame] @app/args.ts:11
  locals: qty = NaN   // Number("x")
price: price(qty) [frame] @cart/price.ts:30
  locals: unit = 4.5
  locals: total = NaN
!print: printReceipt(total) [frame] @cart/receipt.ts:8 # prints "Total: NaN"
frames: main > parse > price > print
main > parse | argv | The flag value arrives as the string "x".
parse > price | qty | Number("x") is NaN, and nothing checks it.
!price > print | total | NaN times anything is NaN, so the receipt prints NaN.

== graph Sequence
view: seq
browser: Browser
api: API [service] @api/checkout.ts:14
db: Postgres [store]
pay: Payment provider
mail: Email queue [queue]
browser -> api: POST /checkout
  at: 0ms
api -> db: SELECT cart
  at: 12ms
db -> api: 3 rows
  at: 30ms
api -> pay: charge
  at: 34ms
pay -> api: ok
  at: 720ms
api ~> mail: receipt
  at: 730ms
api -> browser: 200
  at: 840ms
browser > api > db > api | cart | Reading the cart takes 18 ms.
api > pay > api | charge | The charge is synchronous: 686 of the 840 ms are spent waiting on it.
api > mail | receipt | The receipt is queued, so the email does not hold the response.

== graph States
view: states
queued: queued [state] @jobs/export.ts:20
running: running [state] @jobs/export.ts:41
  does: heartbeat every 10 s
*blocked: blocked [state] @jobs/export.ts:77 # rate-limited
done: done [state]
!dead: dead letter [state] @jobs/export.ts:90 # after 5 tries
queued -> running: picked up
running -> running: heartbeat
running -> blocked: 429
blocked -> queued: retry, backoff 2^n s
running -> done: finished
blocked -> dead: 5th failure
ok: queued > running => done | job 7 | Picked up, runs, done.
retry: queued > running > blocked > queued | job 8 | Rate-limited: it goes back to queued with backoff.
!giveup: running > blocked => dead | job 9 | After five tries it lands in dead letter and stops.

== graph Before and after
ranks: Caller | Lookup | Store | Result
-- Caller
api: GET /user/:id @api/user.ts:12
-- Lookup
+cache: Redis cache [store] @cache/user.ts:8 # TTL 60 s
-direct: direct read @api/user.ts:20
-- Store
db: Postgres [store] @db/users.ts:30
-- Result
user: User JSON
-before: api > direct > db => user | id | Before: every request read Postgres.
+hit: api > cache => user | id | After: a hit returns from Redis and skips the database.
+miss: api > cache > db => user | id | A miss still reads Postgres, then fills the cache.

== graph Lanes
ranks: Request | Service | Payment | Store | Report
-- Request
cart: Cart page @shop/cart.ts:8
  lane: Storefront team
-- Service
checkout: Checkout API @shop/checkout.ts:30
  lane: Storefront team
-- Payment
charge: Charge card @pay/charge.ts:44
  lane: Payments team
-- Store
ledger: Ledger entry @pay/ledger.ts:19
  lane: Payments team
-- Report
report: Revenue report @data/report.sql:1
  lane: Data team
buy: cart > checkout > charge => ledger | order | An order crosses from storefront into payments at the charge.
rev: ledger > report | ledger rows | The nightly report reads the ledger: a second boundary.

== graph Coverage grid
ranks: Writer | Event | Cache
-- Writer
signup: Signup flow @auth/signup.ts:20
edit: Profile edit @profile/edit.ts:33
admin: Admin console @admin/users.ts:51
*sync: Nightly HR sync [job] @jobs/hr_sync.ts:12
-- Event
changed: UserChanged [event] @events/user.ts:6
?direct: direct SQL update [event] @jobs/hr_sync.ts:40 # no event emitted
-- Cache
refresh: Cache refreshed @cache/profile.ts:18
stale: Cache stays stale
s_name: signup > changed => refresh
e_name: edit > changed => refresh
e_avatar: edit > changed => refresh
a_role: admin > changed => refresh
h_title: sync > direct =| stale
h_role: sync > direct =| stale | role | The HR sync writes role with direct SQL, so no event fires and the cache keeps the old role.

== cover Cached field × writer
columns: Writer
name <- s_name, e_name
avatar <- e_avatar
role <- a_role, h_role
title <- h_title
